"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[10664],{710664:e=>{e.exports='# Kafka Streaming - Python\n\nIngesting data from Apache Kafka using Python in Spark Declarative Pipelines.\n\n---\n\n## Basic Kafka Ingestion\n\n```python\nfrom pyspark import pipelines as dp\nfrom pyspark.sql import functions as F\nfrom pyspark.sql.dataframe import DataFrame\n\n@dp.table(name="bronze_kafka_events")\ndef bronze_kafka_events() -> DataFrame:\n    """Ingest raw events from Kafka. Starts from the earliest offset by default."""\n    kafka_brokers = spark.conf.get("kafka_brokers")\n    return (\n        spark.readStream\n        .format("kafka")\n        .option("kafka.bootstrap.servers", kafka_brokers)\n        .option("subscribe", "events-topic")\n        .option("startingOffsets", "earliest")     # Replay all data for tests/demos\n        .option("failOnDataLoss", "false")         # Prevent failure if Kafka retention expires\n        .load()\n        .selectExpr(\n            "CAST(key AS STRING) AS event_key",\n            "CAST(value AS STRING) AS event_value",\n            "topic",\n            "partition",\n            "offset",\n            "timestamp AS kafka_timestamp"\n        )\n        .withColumn("_ingested_at", F.current_timestamp())\n    )\n```\n\n---\n\n## Configuration Options\n\n| Option                                        | Description                                       | Example                         |\n| --------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `kafka.bootstrap.servers`                     | Kafka broker addresses                            | `\'broker1:9092,broker2:9092\'`   |\n| `subscribe`                                   | Topic(s) to subscribe                             | `\'topic1\'` or `\'topic1,topic2\'` |\n| `subscribePattern`                            | Topic pattern (regex)                             | `\'events-.*\'`                   |\n| `startingOffsets`                             | Where to start reading                            | `\'earliest\'`, `\'latest\'`        |\n| `failOnDataLoss`                              | Prevent failure if offsets expire                 | `\'false\'`                       |\n| `databricks.serviceCredential`                | Unity Catalog service credential name             | `\'my-credential\'`               |\n| `kafka.ssl.endpoint.identification.algorithm` | SSL hostname verification (prevents MITM attacks) | `\'https\'`                       |\n| `kafka.request.timeout.ms`                    | Request timeout (prevents hanging connections)    | `\'60000\'`                       |\n| `kafka.session.timeout.ms`                    | Consumer session timeout (controls rebalancing)   | `\'30000\'`                       |\n| `kafka.group.id`                              | Consumer group ID (for offset tracking)           | `\'my-consumer-group\'`           |\n\n---\n\n## Parse JSON Payload\n\n### With Schema Definition\n\n```python\nfrom pyspark.sql.types import StructType, StructField, StringType, TimestampType, MapType\n\nevent_schema = StructType([\n    StructField("event_id", StringType()),\n    StructField("event_type", StringType()),\n    StructField("user_id", StringType()),\n    StructField("timestamp", TimestampType()),\n    StructField("payload", MapType(StringType(), StringType()))\n])\n\n@dp.table(name="silver_events")\ndef silver_events():\n    return (\n        spark.readStream.table("bronze_kafka_events")\n        .withColumn("data", F.from_json("event_value", event_schema))\n        .select(\n            "data.event_id",\n            "data.event_type",\n            "data.user_id",\n            F.col("data.timestamp").alias("event_timestamp"),\n            "data.payload",\n            "kafka_timestamp",\n            "_ingested_at"\n        )\n    )\n```\n\n---\n\n## Multiple Topics\n\n### Subscribe to Multiple Topics\n\n```python\n.option("subscribe", "orders,customers,products")\n```\n\n### Use Topic Pattern\n\n```python\n.option("subscribePattern", "prod-events-.*")\n```\n\n### Route by Topic\n\n```python\n@dp.table(name="bronze_all_events")\ndef bronze_all_events():\n    return (\n        spark.readStream.format("kafka")\n        .option("kafka.bootstrap.servers", spark.conf.get("kafka_brokers"))\n        .option("subscribe", "orders,customers")\n        .load()\n    )\n\n@dp.table(name="silver_orders")\ndef silver_orders():\n    return spark.readStream.table("bronze_all_events").filter(F.col("topic") == "orders")\n\n@dp.table(name="silver_customers")\ndef silver_customers():\n    return spark.readStream.table("bronze_all_events").filter(F.col("topic") == "customers")\n```\n\n---\n\n## Authentication\n\n### Service Credential (Recommended)\n\nUnity Catalog service credentials are the preferred authentication method for Kafka on Databricks. They eliminate JAAS configuration, work on shared clusters and serverless compute, and handle credential lifecycle automatically. Supported for AWS MSK, Azure Event Hubs, and GCP Managed Kafka.\n\n```python\nkafka_options = {\n    "kafka.bootstrap.servers": spark.conf.get("kafka_brokers"),\n    "subscribe": "events-topic",\n    "databricks.serviceCredential": "<service-credential-name>",\n}\n\nreturn (\n    spark.readStream\n    .format("kafka")\n    .options(**kafka_options)\n    .load()\n)\n```\n\nWhen using a service credential, the following options are **not needed**: `kafka.sasl.mechanism`, `kafka.sasl.jaas.config`, `kafka.security.protocol`, `kafka.sasl.client.callback.handler.class`.\n\n### SCRAM-SHA-256 Authentication\n\nSCRAM-SHA-256 uses challenge-response authentication and never transmits passwords in cleartext, making it more secure than SASL/PLAIN. Use this when service credentials are not available. Not supported by Azure Event Hubs — use SASL/PLAIN with `$ConnectionString` for Event Hubs.\n\n```python\nkafka_options = {\n    "kafka.bootstrap.servers": spark.conf.get("kafka_brokers"),\n    "kafka.security.protocol": "SASL_SSL",\n    "kafka.sasl.mechanism": "SCRAM-SHA-256",\n    "kafka.sasl.jaas.config": f\'kafkashaded.org.apache.kafka.common.security.scram.ScramLoginModule required username="{dbutils.secrets.get(scope="kafka", key="username")}" password="{dbutils.secrets.get(scope="kafka", key="password")}";\',\n    "kafka.ssl.endpoint.identification.algorithm": "https",\n}\n\nreturn (\n    spark.readStream\n    .format("kafka")\n    .options(**kafka_options)\n    .option("subscribe", "events")\n    .load()\n)\n```\n\n### SASL/Plain Authentication\n\n```python\n@dp.table(name="bronze_secure_events")\ndef bronze_secure_events():\n    username = dbutils.secrets.get(scope="kafka", key="username")\n    password = dbutils.secrets.get(scope="kafka", key="password")\n\n    jaas_config = f\'kafkashaded.org.apache.kafka.common.security.plain.PlainLoginModule required username="{username}" password="{password}";\'\n\n    return (\n        spark.readStream\n        .format("kafka")\n        .option("kafka.bootstrap.servers", spark.conf.get("kafka_brokers"))\n        .option("subscribe", "events")\n        .option("kafka.security.protocol", "SASL_SSL")\n        .option("kafka.sasl.mechanism", "PLAIN")\n        .option("kafka.sasl.jaas.config", jaas_config)\n        .load()\n    )\n```\n\n### Azure Event Hubs (Kafka API)\n\n```python\n@dp.table(name="bronze_eventhub_events")\ndef bronze_eventhub_events():\n    namespace = spark.conf.get("eventhub_namespace")\n    eventhub_name = spark.conf.get("eventhub_name")\n    connection_string = dbutils.secrets.get(scope="eventhub", key="connection-string")\n\n    jaas_config = f\'kafkashaded.org.apache.kafka.common.security.plain.PlainLoginModule required username="$ConnectionString" password="{connection_string}";\'\n\n    return (\n        spark.readStream\n        .format("kafka")\n        .option("kafka.bootstrap.servers", f"{namespace}.servicebus.windows.net:9093")\n        .option("subscribe", eventhub_name)\n        .option("kafka.security.protocol", "SASL_SSL")\n        .option("kafka.sasl.mechanism", "PLAIN")\n        .option("kafka.sasl.jaas.config", jaas_config)\n        .load()\n    )\n```\n\n---\n\n## Read/Write Options Separation\n\nConsumer-only options like `kafka.group.id` and `kafka.session.timeout.ms` cause errors when used with Kafka producers. Use separate option dictionaries for reads and writes.\n\n```python\n# With service credentials - full options for READS\nkafka_read_options = {\n    "kafka.bootstrap.servers": spark.conf.get("kafka_brokers"),\n    "databricks.serviceCredential": "<service-credential-name>",\n    "kafka.request.timeout.ms": "60000",\n    "kafka.session.timeout.ms": "30000",\n    "kafka.group.id": "my-pipeline-consumer-group",\n}\n\n# For WRITES - filter out consumer-only options\nkafka_write_options = {\n    k: v for k, v in kafka_read_options.items()\n    if k not in ["kafka.group.id", "kafka.session.timeout.ms"]\n}\n```\n\nIf service credentials are not available, use SASL options instead:\n\n```python\n# With SASL - full options for READS\nkafka_read_options = {\n    "kafka.bootstrap.servers": spark.conf.get("kafka_brokers"),\n    "kafka.security.protocol": "SASL_SSL",\n    "kafka.sasl.mechanism": "SCRAM-SHA-256",\n    "kafka.sasl.jaas.config": f\'kafkashaded.org.apache.kafka.common.security.scram.ScramLoginModule required username="{dbutils.secrets.get(scope="kafka", key="username")}" password="{dbutils.secrets.get(scope="kafka", key="password")}";\',\n    "kafka.ssl.endpoint.identification.algorithm": "https",\n    "kafka.request.timeout.ms": "60000",\n    "kafka.session.timeout.ms": "30000",\n    "kafka.group.id": "my-pipeline-consumer-group",\n}\n\n# For WRITES - filter out consumer-only options\nkafka_write_options = {\n    k: v for k, v in kafka_read_options.items()\n    if k not in ["kafka.group.id", "kafka.session.timeout.ms"]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Pipeline Parameters\n\nAccess configuration in Python:\n\n```python\nkafka_brokers = spark.conf.get("kafka_brokers")\ntopic_name = spark.conf.get("topic_name", "default-topic")  # With default\n```\n\nDefine in pipeline settings (YAML):\n\n```yaml\nconfiguration:\n  kafka_brokers: broker1:9092,broker2:9092\n  topic_name: events\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Issues\n\n| Issue                 | Solution                                            |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| Connection refused    | Verify `kafka.bootstrap.servers` and network access |\n| Authentication failed | Check secrets and JAAS config                       |\n| No data received      | Verify topic exists; check `startingOffsets`        |\n| Schema mismatch       | Use explicit schema definition                      |\n'}}]);
